      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14, and D23; no supply, driver, or other pin is connected to it.",
      "expected": "A 3.3 V LED supply or switched 3.3 V driver should be connected to this net so the Ethernet/activity LEDs can conduct through their current-limiting resistors to the open-collector outputs.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"71\") (name \"ETH_LEDG\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"Module1\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"Ethernet_nLED2(3.3v)\") (pintype \"output\")) (node (ref \"R3\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 have no anode voltage, so the Pi activity and Ethernet link/activity LEDs will not illuminate.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D30", "R60"],
      "pins": ["D30.2", "D30.4", "R60.1", "R60.2"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K2)"],
      "observed": "D30 pin 4 (A2) is connected to ESTOP_OUT, and D30 pin 2 (K2) is connected through R60 back to the same ESTOP_OUT node.",
      "expected": "The LED should be connected between a voltage source and ESTOP_OUT, for example A2 to a 3.3 V rail and K2 through R60 to ESTOP_OUT, or A2 to ESTOP_OUT and K2 through R60 to GND, so ESTOP_OUT can drive the LED.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"67\") (name \"ESTOP_OUT\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"J13\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U36\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") (pintype \"output\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"129\") (name \"Net-(D30-K2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"K2\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"R60\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The second channel of D30 has both ends tied to the same net through a resistor, so it cannot light; the e-stop/CAN status indication is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows two unambiguous LED-drive faults: a floating /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW supply net and D30's second LED tied from ESTOP_OUT back to ESTOP_OUT through R60. These would make the board behave differently from a normally powered LED indication circuit."
}

